WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.797
<v Examiner>What is the nurse's role with a person whose substance use is a concern?

2
00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:07.563
<v Examiner>Where can a nurse refer them?

3
00:00:07.563 --> 00:00:08.173
<v Examiner>Two marks.

4
00:00:08.623 --> 00:00:12.377
The hook: ask, brief intervention, refer, follow up, advocate.

5
00:00:12.827 --> 00:00:14.998
Her notes list the nurse's role.

6
00:00:14.998 --> 00:00:16.151
Asking about use.

7
00:00:16.151 --> 00:00:17.576
A brief intervention.

8
00:00:17.576 --> 00:00:18.865
Offering referrals.

9
00:00:18.865 --> 00:00:19.747
Following up.

10
00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:20.628
And advocacy.

11
00:00:20.628 --> 00:00:24.902
Before any of it: anyone can take drugs, so avoid stereotyping.

12
00:00:25.352 --> 00:00:27.262
Where to refer, in Auckland.

13
00:00:27.262 --> 00:00:30.127
Community Alcohol and Drug Services, CADS.

14
00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:33.197
Inside it, Te Ātea Marinō, the Māori service.

15
00:00:33.197 --> 00:00:35.038
Tupu, the Pasifika service.

16
00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:37.494
And Altered High, the youth service.

17
00:00:37.494 --> 00:00:40.836
And rehabilitation providers, like Odyssey House.

18
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:46.293
For information: the Drug Foundation, The Level, and Alcohol Drug Help websites.

19
00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:49.772
And because drug use and mental ill health overlap,

20
00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:52.433
think about mental health services too.

21
00:00:53.883 --> 00:00:54.836
Harm reduction.

22
00:00:54.836 --> 00:00:58.459
Reducing the harm for people who are going to use anyway,

23
00:00:58.459 --> 00:01:00.748
instead of only telling them not to.

24
00:01:00.748 --> 00:01:05.388
Her slide calls interactions an opportunity for harm reduction education.

25
00:01:05.388 --> 00:01:09.456
Two examples from Aotearoa, from the articles she points you to.

26
00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:14.986
Drug checking: Know Your Stuff runs free, legal drug checking at festivals and clinics.

27
00:01:14.986 --> 00:01:18.863
New Zealand changed the Misuse of Drugs Act to make it legal,

28
00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:24.584
and when people find out their drug isn't what they thought, more than half don't take it.

29
00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:29.923
And naloxone, the opioid overdose reversal medicine, in the hands of people at risk.

30
00:01:30.373 --> 00:01:30.954
<v Examiner>Once more.

31
00:01:30.954 --> 00:01:33.104
<v Examiner>The nurse's role, and harm reduction.

32
00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:40.831
The nurse's role: don't stereotype; ask about use, give a brief intervention,

33
00:01:40.831 --> 00:01:43.641
offer referrals, follow up, and advocate.

34
00:01:43.641 --> 00:01:49.810
Refer to Community Alcohol and Drug Services: Te Ātea Marinō for Māori, Tupu for Pasifika,

35
00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:54.128
Altered High for youth, or a rehab provider like Odyssey House.

36
00:01:54.128 --> 00:02:00.090
Harm reduction: make use safer for people who will use anyway, like free drug checking,

37
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.723
or naloxone for people at risk of an opioid overdose.
